# ─── Cloudflare Zero Trust Access Policy ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# How it works:
#   1. Any unauthenticated request → Cloudflare blocks it at the edge.
#   2. The user opens https://beeftv.<YOUR_DOMAIN>
#   3. Cloudflare presents a login page (email + one-time passcode).
#   4. After confirming their email, traffic is routed through to the web server.
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. In the Zero Trust dashboard (dash.cloudflare.com → Zero Trust):
#        • Create a tunnel named "beeftv-local" and note the TUNNEL ID.
#        • Add a DNS CNAME: beeftv.<YOUR_DOMAIN> → <tunnel-id>.cfargotunnel.com
#        • In Access → Applications → Add an application → Self-hosted
#          → configure as shown below.
#   2. In Access → Access policies: the "Allow" rule must list the user's email.
#      The "Block" default rule cannot be removed; everything not explicitly
#      allowed is blocked.
#   3. Set the "Application domain" to beeftf.<YOUR_DOMAIN>.
#
# NOTE: Cloudflare Free plan supports Zero Trust Access with email OTP
#       for up to 3 applications. No credit card required.

{
  "name": "beeftv-local",
  "status": "active",
  "type": "localhost",
  "session_duration": "24h",
  "policies": [
    {
      "name": "Owner access",
      "decision": "allow",
      "include": [
        {
          "email": {
            "email": "OWNER@YOUR_DOMAIN.com"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Deny all others",
      "decision": "block",
      "include": [
        {
          "emails": null
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
